// The battle code, fifth pass (slice battle5; docs/ANALYSIS/21_battle.md, game/include/p3fes/game/battle5.h for the
// layouts and the battle state a co-op server would own): the battle panel command / message / list / dialog /
// one-more modules, the op_*.c screens and their fade, the result screen's persona sequence and panels,
// the sprite-sheet quads, the unit geometry / walk / model / motion helpers and packet callbacks, the action states
// (turn start, command, all-out attack, end, remove) and the skill resolution, the formation placement, the camera
// shots, the lights, the navigator and support lines, the battle sound requests and voice line pickers, the cut-in
// packets and the boss rules by encounter. Every function the battle replay or the Tartarus climb reaches (a
// first-call probe) that no slice had replaced; still-recompiled callees are reached through their gen:: entry points.
// The bodies are p3fes_handgen's (frame, spills, $ra links, every register, cycle charges, check points); this file
// names their offsets and gives each its role -- proposed names in brackets (ADR-0009), symbols in code are
// functions.json's.
